WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:38.729 --> 00:00:42.298
That feeling of just knowing
a game is right for you

00:00:42.432 --> 00:00:45.234
when you first lay eyes on it
is such a great feeling.

00:00:45.369 --> 00:00:47.070
The thing that happens is

00:00:47.204 --> 00:00:51.474
you start to feel the excitement
just build up.

00:00:51.608 --> 00:00:55.178
I'm thinking about it all the
time, even in my sleep.

00:01:00.517 --> 00:01:02.352
-I play video games
because I love stories.

00:01:04.288 --> 00:01:07.423
-Experiencing worlds that you
can't experience as yourself.

00:01:07.557 --> 00:01:10.727
-I guess video games allow me
to be what I can't.

00:01:10.861 --> 00:01:12.696
It's fiction, but it's not.

00:01:12.829 --> 00:01:15.598
-You come home,
log on to your PC,

00:01:15.732 --> 00:01:17.601
and disappear
into a different world.

00:01:17.734 --> 00:01:20.003
-I am a part of
something bigger,

00:01:20.137 --> 00:01:23.273
a part of something beautiful.

00:01:24.074 --> 00:01:26.843
-As an autistic person,
video games gave me a place

00:01:26.977 --> 00:01:31.048
where I could be in a world
that made sense to me.

00:01:32.482 --> 00:01:34.550
-I will tell you that all of my
family play video games.

00:01:34.685 --> 00:01:35.786
-Me and my brothers,

00:01:35.919 --> 00:01:37.854
we would share
the computer one hour at a time.

00:01:41.124 --> 00:01:42.592
I'm really enjoying
playing video games with my dad.

00:01:42.726 --> 00:01:44.827
-...my children.
-...my little sister.

00:01:44.961 --> 00:01:47.431
That connection
between video games

00:01:47.564 --> 00:01:49.699
allowing us
to converse with each other

00:01:49.833 --> 00:01:51.367
added a lot to our relationship.

00:01:51.501 --> 00:01:53.203
-Games like World of Warcraft
let me meet people

00:01:53.337 --> 00:01:55.905
that I probably
never would have.

00:01:56.039 --> 00:01:57.473
-I can honestly say
that I've met

00:01:57.607 --> 00:02:01.077
some of my best friends
through playing games.

00:02:01.211 --> 00:02:05.314
-We have this connection that
allows us to share our joys,

00:02:05.449 --> 00:02:08.985
to share our achievements,
to share our growth together.

00:02:09.119 --> 00:02:10.953
-Every time I'm able
to achieve something,

00:02:11.088 --> 00:02:12.555
I'm able to make myself proud.

00:02:12.689 --> 00:02:15.391
-Killing Heroic Blackhand

00:02:15.525 --> 00:02:18.228
back in Warlords of Draenor
was one of my favorite memories.

00:02:18.362 --> 00:02:20.063
-I managed to find
that one hidden Pylon

00:02:20.197 --> 00:02:22.465
with my one Mutalisk.

00:02:22.599 --> 00:02:25.835
-We beat Hardcore
Inferno Diablo.

00:02:25.969 --> 00:02:28.771
-I was able to hit Gold in
Competitive in Overwatch.

00:02:28.905 --> 00:02:31.173
-I had someone say,
"Oh, I can't lose to a girl."

00:02:31.308 --> 00:02:32.775
And I beat that guy.

00:02:32.909 --> 00:02:38.248
I was able to slay this warlock
as a little gnome holy priest,

00:02:38.382 --> 00:02:39.682
freaking out
and screaming the whole time.

00:02:39.816 --> 00:02:42.185
-The adrenaline through my body
was going crazy!

00:02:50.627 --> 00:02:52.829
-"I killed the Lich King!
I killed the Lich King!"

00:03:01.638 --> 00:03:04.674
-Many years ago, I was doing a
quest in Terokkar Forest,

00:03:04.808 --> 00:03:06.008
and a lovely little mage
came up and said,

00:03:06.143 --> 00:03:07.243
"Would you like a hand?"

00:03:07.377 --> 00:03:08.978
They helped me
for the rest of the day.

00:03:09.980 --> 00:03:11.114
We've been married now
for over a decade.

00:03:11.248 --> 00:03:13.616
-Those video games
filled a void.

00:03:13.750 --> 00:03:15.785
They filled the friendships
I didn't have.

00:03:15.919 --> 00:03:19.456
There isn't a huge
LGBTQIA+ community in my city,

00:03:19.589 --> 00:03:21.291
so when I was able
to play a video game,

00:03:21.425 --> 00:03:24.227
I was able to start talking
with people

00:03:24.361 --> 00:03:25.695
who didn't really care
that I was a gay male.

00:03:26.563 --> 00:03:28.198
-Video games were my escape.

00:03:29.166 --> 00:03:31.701
When I was a teenager
my dad was diagnosed with ALS,

00:03:31.835 --> 00:03:35.705
and I looked to video games
as a way

00:03:35.839 --> 00:03:37.607
to escape
from that sort of reality.

00:03:38.575 --> 00:03:39.675
Everything happens for a reason,

00:03:39.810 --> 00:03:42.512
and I'm glad video games
were there for me.

00:03:42.646 --> 00:03:43.580
I'll never stop playing
video games.

00:03:43.713 --> 00:03:45.348
-There's no way.

00:03:45.482 --> 00:03:47.183
-I imagine myself, one day,

00:03:47.317 --> 00:03:49.285
being an 80-year-old
grandpa gamer.

00:03:49.419 --> 00:03:51.087
-Playing video games
has shaped me.

00:03:51.221 --> 00:03:54.090
I don't think I would be
who I am today.

00:03:54.224 --> 00:03:57.727
-My passion, my interest,
my excitement, they belong.

00:03:57.861 --> 00:03:59.295
-Video games opened,
for me, the world...

00:03:59.429 --> 00:04:01.998
-...and because of that,
I'm forever thankful.

00:04:02.132 --> 00:04:04.467
-And I can't wait to see
what the next generation holds.

00:04:04.601 --> 00:04:06.403
# EPIC ORCHESTRAL MUSIC

00:04:31.361 --> 00:04:32.429
# MUSIC CRESCENDOS

00:04:44.608 --> 00:04:47.344
Welcome to BlizzConline,

00:04:47.477 --> 00:04:51.247
a celebration of 30 years
of Blizzard communities

00:04:51.381 --> 00:04:53.683
and 30 years of Blizzard games.

00:04:55.886 --> 00:04:59.089
Thirty years is so many years,

00:04:59.956 --> 00:05:03.526
and last year maybe felt
like one of the longest of all.

00:05:03.660 --> 00:05:04.760
But throughout the years

00:05:04.895 --> 00:05:06.695
of Blizzard Entertainment,

00:05:06.830 --> 00:05:09.198
from 1991 to today,

00:05:09.332 --> 00:05:11.934
many of us can associate
certain games

00:05:12.068 --> 00:05:14.704
with milestones in our lives.

00:05:14.838 --> 00:05:17.273
Maybe you were a little kid

00:05:17.407 --> 00:05:19.175
the first time you played
The Lost Vikings,

00:05:20.644 --> 00:05:23.513
or in high school when you first
played a Diablo game,

00:05:25.348 --> 00:05:26.616
or maybe you met your partner

00:05:26.750 --> 00:05:29.285
while you were playing
World of Warcraft.

00:05:29.419 --> 00:05:31.787
That's the awesome thing
about video games.

00:05:31.922 --> 00:05:33.623
They give us experiences

00:05:33.757 --> 00:05:36.893
that are relevant
to the times in our lives,

00:05:37.027 --> 00:05:40.296
and experiences
that we carry forward with us.

00:05:40.430 --> 00:05:43.600
Games are here
for us during good times,

00:05:43.733 --> 00:05:46.936
and they're here for us
even when we feel alone,

00:05:47.070 --> 00:05:49.072
or maybe uncertain.

00:05:49.839 --> 00:05:50.941
Games are coming home:

00:05:52.008 --> 00:05:52.875
familiar,

00:05:53.009 --> 00:05:54.710
comfortable,

00:05:54.844 --> 00:05:55.978
with a connection

00:05:56.112 --> 00:05:58.814
and a sense of belonging.

00:05:58.949 --> 00:06:01.784
And while many of us
spent most of 2020

00:06:01.918 --> 00:06:04.887
in our actual real-life homes,

00:06:05.021 --> 00:06:09.325
games became even more
of a place to get away,

00:06:09.459 --> 00:06:11.227
to be free
from outside concerns...

00:06:12.195 --> 00:06:13.463
even if just for a little while.

00:06:14.364 --> 00:06:17.567
So... this is pretty weird.

00:06:19.035 --> 00:06:22.238
Usually when we start BlizzCon,

00:06:22.372 --> 00:06:25.574
the opening call is
to my favorite Warcraft faction,

00:06:25.709 --> 00:06:26.742
the Alliance.

00:06:26.876 --> 00:06:28.411
# ORCHESTRAL MUSIC

00:06:28.545 --> 00:06:30.913
Or is my favorite faction
the Horde?

00:06:31.047 --> 00:06:31.915
I get confused.

00:06:33.550 --> 00:06:37.086
Usually I'd be speaking
to 40,000 of you in person

00:06:37.220 --> 00:06:39.255
at the Anaheim
Convention Center,

00:06:39.389 --> 00:06:41.424
and millions of you
around the world.

00:06:42.359 --> 00:06:45.395
And usually that would be a
perfect way to celebrate.

00:06:48.298 --> 00:06:50.600
But nothing about the last year
has been usual.

00:06:52.535 --> 00:06:55.505
The pandemic has been
hard on everyone,

00:06:55.639 --> 00:06:57.240
and for many different reasons.

00:06:58.975 --> 00:07:02.178
But if there's one thing that
the last year has taught us,

00:07:02.312 --> 00:07:04.347
it's that being apart physically

00:07:04.481 --> 00:07:07.917
doesn't stop us
from moving forward.

00:07:08.952 --> 00:07:11.854
It doesn't stop us
from connecting

00:07:11.988 --> 00:07:14.624
with our player friends
around the world,

00:07:14.758 --> 00:07:17.293
diving in as warriors
and heroes...

00:07:19.429 --> 00:07:21.131
and checking on each other
as humans.

00:07:22.666 --> 00:07:28.104
It doesn't stop us from sharing
our latest epic gaming story,

00:07:28.238 --> 00:07:29.973
or celebrating those of others.

00:07:32.008 --> 00:07:34.878
Games continue to unite us.

00:07:36.513 --> 00:07:38.981
Now, to be honest,

00:07:40.250 --> 00:07:42.852
I wasn't sure how well
Blizzard could work from home.

00:07:43.820 --> 00:07:45.955
There are thousands of people,

00:07:46.089 --> 00:07:47.690
all needing to work together

00:07:47.824 --> 00:07:49.626
in creating our universes,

00:07:49.759 --> 00:07:52.128
games and experiences.

00:07:52.996 --> 00:07:54.864
Never has it felt more true

00:07:54.998 --> 00:07:57.233
that it takes a Blizzard
to make a Blizzard game.

00:07:58.768 --> 00:08:01.303
And in 2020, it became clear

00:08:01.438 --> 00:08:04.140
that the magic of creating
at Blizzard

00:08:04.274 --> 00:08:07.410
isn't just tied
to a physical location.

00:08:07.544 --> 00:08:09.812
It's tied to the people
who work here,

00:08:09.946 --> 00:08:14.084
and I continue to be so proud of
each and every one of them.

00:08:14.818 --> 00:08:15.752
Thank you, Blizzard.

00:08:16.720 --> 00:08:19.055
We create these games

00:08:19.189 --> 00:08:22.225
and pour all of our energy
and heart into them,

00:08:22.358 --> 00:08:25.095
but it is you,
the Blizzard community,

00:08:25.929 --> 00:08:27.196
that brings them to life.

00:08:27.330 --> 00:08:30.766
And that's why BlizzConline
is a celebration of you:

00:08:30.900 --> 00:08:32.768
the guild leaders,

00:08:32.902 --> 00:08:34.103
healers,

00:08:34.237 --> 00:08:35.605
DPS,

00:08:35.739 --> 00:08:36.840
tanks,

00:08:37.440 --> 00:08:38.841
innkeepers,

00:08:38.975 --> 00:08:40.409
Zerg,

00:08:40.543 --> 00:08:40.876
Terran,

00:08:41.010 --> 00:08:42.145
Protoss,

00:08:43.046 --> 00:08:43.580
Blackwatch,

00:08:44.481 --> 00:08:45.582
Shimada,

00:08:46.649 --> 00:08:48.417
the heroes of Sanctuary,

00:08:48.551 --> 00:08:49.586
and of the Storm.

00:08:51.221 --> 00:08:53.589
These next few days are for you,

00:08:53.723 --> 00:08:54.524
our Blizzard community.

00:08:57.127 --> 00:08:58.094
For World of Warcraft,

00:08:59.329 --> 00:09:01.430
we'll be showing you what's next

00:09:01.564 --> 00:09:03.933
for both Shadowlands
and Classic.

00:09:05.301 --> 00:09:08.638
I'm sure you're all burning
in anticipation for that one.

00:09:10.106 --> 00:09:13.676
Hearthstone is getting back to
its roots in a major way.

00:09:13.810 --> 00:09:15.178
We can't wait to show you how.

00:09:18.681 --> 00:09:22.051
We also have news
for our Diablo community.

00:09:22.185 --> 00:09:24.119
Some of you were able to
dip your toes

00:09:24.254 --> 00:09:26.221
into the depths of hell

00:09:26.356 --> 00:09:28.791
in the Diablo Immortal
Technical Alpha.

00:09:28.925 --> 00:09:33.296
Personally, I really enjoyed
seeing players embrace

00:09:33.429 --> 00:09:36.032
the multiplayer aspect
of meeting in town.

00:09:37.600 --> 00:09:39.903
We can't wait for more of you
to get your hands on it.

00:09:41.271 --> 00:09:43.706
So, it's only the beginning
of the year,

00:09:43.840 --> 00:09:46.442
and already there is so much to
look forward to,

00:09:46.576 --> 00:09:48.745
even though we can't yet
be together in person.

00:09:50.680 --> 00:09:54.217
The Overwatch League will be
kicking things off in spring,

00:09:54.350 --> 00:09:57.987
and we'll be watching closely to
see if the San Francisco Shock

00:09:58.121 --> 00:10:00.390
can continue
their championship run.

00:10:03.193 --> 00:10:05.828
World of Warcraft
esports is back,

00:10:05.962 --> 00:10:07.797
with the Arena World
Championship

00:10:07.931 --> 00:10:10.799
and Mythic Dungeon International

00:10:10.934 --> 00:10:12.569
already in full swing
in Shadowlands.

00:10:14.971 --> 00:10:18.340
StarCraft II and Warcraft III
esports are going strong

00:10:18.474 --> 00:10:20.910
with our friends
at the ESL Pro Tour.

00:10:22.879 --> 00:10:26.149
And qualifiers
are already underway

00:10:26.282 --> 00:10:32.255
for the first online stop of the
2021 Hearthstone Masters Tour,

00:10:32.388 --> 00:10:34.924
with the first event taking
place next month.

00:10:37.560 --> 00:10:39.495
But before
we get too far ahead...

00:10:41.731 --> 00:10:43.700
let's take a look one last time

00:10:44.901 --> 00:10:47.203
to when times
were a little simpler.

00:10:48.404 --> 00:10:50.506
In the early 1990s,
the Internet was a baby.

00:10:51.674 --> 00:10:54.877
CD sales had finally eclipsed
cassette tapes.

00:10:55.011 --> 00:10:58.881
A cassette tape, it's a
rectangular piece of plastic,

00:10:59.015 --> 00:11:01.784
and there's tape inside that
music would get recorded on,

00:11:01.918 --> 00:11:03.686
and sometimes
you needed a pencil

00:11:03.820 --> 00:11:05.354
to wind it and make it tight.

00:11:05.488 --> 00:11:06.155
I know, it sounds crazy.

00:11:07.090 --> 00:11:10.292
We were all playing video games
on Super Nintendo,

00:11:10.426 --> 00:11:13.295
Sega Genesis, DOS, or Mac/PCs.

00:11:14.264 --> 00:11:17.700
I personally was a master of
CONFIG.SYS and AUTOEXEC.BAT.

00:11:18.668 --> 00:11:21.971
So many simple things,
in simple times.

00:11:23.773 --> 00:11:24.974
If only we could relive them.

00:11:26.342 --> 00:11:28.378
WIND WHOOSHING

00:11:29.112 --> 00:11:32.748
# SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC

00:11:32.882 --> 00:11:33.616
# '90s ARCADE MUSIC

00:11:33.750 --> 00:11:35.084
VOICEOVER: The stage is set.

00:11:36.219 --> 00:11:36.953
The green flag drops!

00:11:38.054 --> 00:11:40.790
Let the carnage begin!

00:11:42.725 --> 00:11:44.527
Holy Toledo!

00:11:46.462 --> 00:11:48.131
What a collection!

00:11:58.374 --> 00:11:59.509
Now we're talking!

00:12:06.215 --> 00:12:07.250
What a play!

00:12:15.892 --> 00:12:17.860
Crank up the volume!

00:12:18.695 --> 00:12:20.162
# '90s ARCADE
ROCK 'N' ROLL MUSIC

00:12:20.296 --> 00:12:21.397
Unbelievable!

00:12:28.571 --> 00:12:29.739
Whoa!

00:12:51.561 --> 00:12:53.929
The Blizzard Arcade Collection,

00:12:54.063 --> 00:12:57.900
featuring The Lost Vikings, Rock
n' Roll Racing, and Blackthorne.

00:12:58.901 --> 00:13:02.972
These are ports of the games
just as you remember them,

00:13:03.106 --> 00:13:05.875
allowing you to relive
the original experience

00:13:06.009 --> 00:13:09.445
of all three titles
in 13 different languages,

00:13:10.613 --> 00:13:12.982
with a couple of
quality-of-life upgrades.

00:13:14.017 --> 00:13:17.119
As an example,
we include very modern,

00:13:17.253 --> 00:13:18.488
cutting-edge functionality

00:13:18.621 --> 00:13:21.156
that wasn't available
in the early '90s:

00:13:21.290 --> 00:13:24.059
both saving
and loading of games.

00:13:24.193 --> 00:13:25.561
And for those of you
who purchased

00:13:25.695 --> 00:13:28.063
any Blizzard digital
anniversary bundle

00:13:28.197 --> 00:13:29.565
via Battle.net,

00:13:29.699 --> 00:13:33.235
you'll automatically receive
the Blizzard Arcade Collection

00:13:33.369 --> 00:13:35.405
on PC today.

00:13:37.473 --> 00:13:40.876
Now, you ready to hear about
some other video games?

00:13:41.944 --> 00:13:43.980
Let's hear what's next
for World of Warcraft.

00:13:45.948 --> 00:13:47.583
# DRAMATIC ORCHESTRAL MUSIC

00:13:58.995 --> 00:14:00.096
SNARLS

00:14:01.864 --> 00:14:03.899
Hello, everyone!

00:14:04.033 --> 00:14:06.001
Thanks for joining us today.

00:14:06.135 --> 00:14:10.006
No matter where you are,
World of Warcraft unites us all.

00:14:11.140 --> 00:14:13.175
Whether you're exploring
the Shadowlands,

00:14:13.309 --> 00:14:15.845
Classic Azeroth, or another part
of the Blizzard universe,

00:14:15.978 --> 00:14:17.680
I'm glad you could make it,

00:14:17.814 --> 00:14:20.516
because we've got
a lot of good stuff to show you.

00:14:21.084 --> 00:14:22.785
But first,

00:14:22.919 --> 00:14:23.920
let's start
with some Covenant pride.

00:14:25.054 --> 00:14:27.090
Kyrian, take flight!

00:14:28.257 --> 00:14:30.793
Night Fae, let the hunt begin!

00:14:31.994 --> 00:14:33.362
Necrolords,

00:14:33.496 --> 00:14:34.363
to war!

00:14:35.832 --> 00:14:37.934
Venthyr, let's party.

00:14:40.236 --> 00:14:43.773
The world has thrown a lot at us
since the last BlizzCon,

00:14:43.906 --> 00:14:47.209
and the thing that's really kept
everyone going on the WoW team

00:14:47.343 --> 00:14:48.511
has been connecting
with all of you.

00:14:49.912 --> 00:14:52.548
The bonds we forge
with our guilds

00:14:52.682 --> 00:14:54.950
and family and friends in WoW

00:14:55.084 --> 00:14:57.620
are powerful and real.

00:14:58.921 --> 00:15:00.289
As WoW enters its 16th year

00:15:00.423 --> 00:15:03.525
and Blizzard celebrates
its 30th anniversary,

00:15:03.659 --> 00:15:06.629
we're so grateful
to have the most dedicated

00:15:06.762 --> 00:15:08.898
and friendly communities
in gaming.

00:15:09.999 --> 00:15:11.868
Let's recap
the events in Azeroth.

00:15:13.069 --> 00:15:15.304
In WoW Classic,
we fought an endless battle

00:15:15.438 --> 00:15:17.573
for Southshore and Tarren Mill.

00:15:17.707 --> 00:15:20.976
We banded together
to open the gates of Ahn'Qiraj,

00:15:21.110 --> 00:15:23.578
and joined forces
to take down Kel'Thuzad

00:15:23.713 --> 00:15:26.149
in his floating citadel
of Naxxramas.

00:15:26.749 --> 00:15:28.016
In Shadowlands,

00:15:28.151 --> 00:15:29.985
we helped our Covenant
recover from the anima drought

00:15:30.119 --> 00:15:32.088
brought on by Sire Denathrius,

00:15:32.221 --> 00:15:34.156
master of the Venthyr

00:15:34.290 --> 00:15:36.359
and traitor
to the Pantheon of Death.

00:15:37.527 --> 00:15:39.561
We survived
the halls of Torghast

00:15:39.695 --> 00:15:40.830
and crafted Legendary gear

00:15:40.963 --> 00:15:42.998
in our efforts
to expel Denathrius

00:15:43.132 --> 00:15:44.634
from his castle lair.

00:15:46.702 --> 00:15:48.337
But innocent souls

00:15:48.471 --> 00:15:51.007
are still wrongfully being sent
to the Maw.

00:15:51.140 --> 00:15:53.242
They face
an eternity of torment,

00:15:53.376 --> 00:15:56.845
and heroes like Anduin
remain chained in its depths.

00:15:57.813 --> 00:16:00.249
The Jailer
continues to grow in power.

00:16:00.383 --> 00:16:02.852
He's preparing
to break free from the Maw

00:16:02.985 --> 00:16:07.023
and complete his plan to unmake
the entire Warcraft universe.

00:16:07.957 --> 00:16:09.591
And Sylvanas,

00:16:09.725 --> 00:16:13.528
you may be wondering what
she's been up to all this time.

00:16:13.663 --> 00:16:16.098
Today, we're excited to unveil

00:16:16.232 --> 00:16:19.034
our first major content update
for Shadowlands:

00:16:19.168 --> 00:16:21.103
Chains of Domination.

00:16:23.239 --> 00:16:25.741
# DRAMATIC ORCHESTRAL MUSIC

00:16:28.744 --> 00:16:30.278
ANDUIN: Look around you!

00:16:31.180 --> 00:16:33.982
What makes you believe
you're not just a weapon

00:16:34.116 --> 00:16:34.716
to achieve his ends?

00:16:34.850 --> 00:16:36.152
Enough!

00:16:37.453 --> 00:16:41.791
Join our cause
or be made to serve.

00:16:42.491 --> 00:16:44.025
Right now,

00:16:44.160 --> 00:16:45.928
you hold all the power.

00:16:48.164 --> 00:16:50.633
Make your choice,
Sylvanas Windrunner.

00:16:53.069 --> 00:16:55.104
WIND WHOOSHING

00:16:58.841 --> 00:17:01.776
THENIOS:
Despite all our efforts,

00:17:01.911 --> 00:17:04.714
the Maw continues to grow.

00:17:05.948 --> 00:17:08.617
What if Denathrius's treachery
is irreparable?

00:17:08.751 --> 00:17:11.053
The Primus is lost,

00:17:11.187 --> 00:17:13.556
and Bastion cannot save
the Shadowlands alone.

00:17:15.024 --> 00:17:16.892
None of this
should have happened.

00:17:17.793 --> 00:17:19.995
Perhaps
the Winter Queen could...

00:17:20.129 --> 00:17:21.230
WINGS FLAPPING

00:17:23.866 --> 00:17:25.668
My Archon...

00:17:25.801 --> 00:17:29.005
a living soul seeks an audience.

00:17:29.138 --> 00:17:29.538
A mortal?

00:17:30.806 --> 00:17:32.441
A king.

00:17:32.575 --> 00:17:34.643
# UPLIFTING ORCHESTRAL MUSIC

00:17:34.777 --> 00:17:35.278
KLEIA: By all our measures...

00:17:37.146 --> 00:17:39.515
one who has spent his life

00:17:39.649 --> 00:17:41.050
striving for justice.

00:17:44.387 --> 00:17:48.057
One who would give anything
to serve his people.

00:17:51.360 --> 00:17:53.262
One whose heart...

00:17:53.729 --> 00:17:55.097
is true.

00:17:55.231 --> 00:17:56.499
Very well.

00:17:57.300 --> 00:17:58.934
He may approach.

00:18:03.973 --> 00:18:05.041
Step forward.

00:18:09.278 --> 00:18:11.981
My Ascended have spoken of you.

00:18:12.915 --> 00:18:14.784
The king
held captive in the Maw.

00:18:16.585 --> 00:18:19.988
That prison
could not hold me forever.

00:18:20.122 --> 00:18:22.425
Why have you come to Bastion?

00:18:23.326 --> 00:18:27.963
You have a key... that I need.

00:18:29.265 --> 00:18:30.866
You...

00:18:32.134 --> 00:18:34.770
will release
this soul from your grasp!

00:18:34.904 --> 00:18:36.705
ANDUIN: No.

00:18:36.839 --> 00:18:39.908
He is bound to me...

00:18:40.042 --> 00:18:45.881
JAILER: ...just as you once
sought to bind your own brother!

00:18:46.749 --> 00:18:48.417
# DRAMATIC ORCHESTRAL MUSIC

00:19:01.297 --> 00:19:02.732
ANDUIN GRUNTS, ARCHON SCREAMS

00:19:09.872 --> 00:19:11.874
PANTING

00:19:13.209 --> 00:19:14.243
GASPS

00:19:19.215 --> 00:19:21.217
# OMINOUS ORCHESTRAL MUSIC

00:19:28.958 --> 00:19:32.762
JAILER: The vessel performed
its part flawlessly.

00:19:36.132 --> 00:19:38.501
Three keys remain.

00:19:40.436 --> 00:19:42.238
Then they will see...

00:19:44.473 --> 00:19:49.412
Death was never meant
to be chained.

00:20:06.829 --> 00:20:08.164
That is so intense.

00:20:09.899 --> 00:20:11.433
I know you probably
have a lot of questions

00:20:11.567 --> 00:20:12.568
about what you just saw,

00:20:12.701 --> 00:20:14.670
and what it means
for the next stage

00:20:14.804 --> 00:20:15.871
of your Shadowlands journey.

00:20:16.005 --> 00:20:18.773
Later today,
my teammates Ion and Jeremy

00:20:18.908 --> 00:20:21.276
will be telling you more about
Chains of Domination

00:20:21.410 --> 00:20:22.911
in our Shadowlands update.

00:20:24.079 --> 00:20:26.615
Please check out
the World of Warcraft channel

00:20:26.749 --> 00:20:27.950
to find out more.

00:20:28.083 --> 00:20:32.053
Next, I'm excited
to share our upcoming

00:20:32.188 --> 00:20:34.556
World of Warcraft
Charity Pet Program.

00:20:34.690 --> 00:20:36.458
We've heard a lot
from our community

00:20:36.592 --> 00:20:38.794
about how much
they love these pets

00:20:38.928 --> 00:20:41.697
and the opportunity
to give to a good cause,

00:20:41.831 --> 00:20:44.733
along with ideas
to make the program even better.

00:20:44.867 --> 00:20:47.570
So during this
upcoming campaign,

00:20:47.703 --> 00:20:50.473
you'll be able to donate
whatever amount you wish

00:20:50.606 --> 00:20:53.308
to directly support
our chosen charity.

00:20:53.442 --> 00:20:55.543
Once donations reach our goal,

00:20:55.678 --> 00:20:57.312
everyone playing
World of Warcraft

00:20:57.446 --> 00:20:59.648
will get a pet
for their collection

00:20:59.782 --> 00:21:01.216
as a thank you,

00:21:02.051 --> 00:21:04.587
whether you were able to
contribute personally or not.

00:21:05.721 --> 00:21:07.823
And to make this
a fun challenge,

00:21:07.957 --> 00:21:09.658
if we reach a stretch goal,

00:21:09.792 --> 00:21:11.393
everyone gets a second pet, too.

00:21:12.528 --> 00:21:12.661
And here they are.

00:21:14.797 --> 00:21:16.832
The first pet is Bananas!

00:21:16.966 --> 00:21:18.033
Literally.

00:21:18.167 --> 00:21:20.769
He was originally available
to a select few

00:21:20.903 --> 00:21:22.170
back in the Burning Crusade era,

00:21:22.304 --> 00:21:25.708
so we're excited to give
everyone a chance to adopt him.

00:21:26.876 --> 00:21:28.243
And if we reach
our stretch goal,

00:21:28.377 --> 00:21:30.412
you'll also get Daisy the Sloth.

00:21:30.546 --> 00:21:31.613
DAISY GRUNTS

00:21:31.747 --> 00:21:32.981
She's an all-new pet

00:21:33.115 --> 00:21:35.684
who will hang around your neck
when you need a hug.

00:21:35.818 --> 00:21:38.687
Your donations during this
campaign will go to support

00:21:38.821 --> 00:21:41.022
the medical humanitarian
organization

00:21:41.156 --> 00:21:42.925
Doctors Without Borders,

00:21:43.792 --> 00:21:45.761
also known by their French name

00:21:45.895 --> 00:21:47.329
Médecins Sans Frontières,
or MSF.

00:21:48.831 --> 00:21:51.867
They're an amazing group doing
important work around the world.

00:21:53.502 --> 00:21:55.871
We're grateful to have
such a generous community,

00:21:56.005 --> 00:21:59.608
and we hope you'll help support
this worthy cause.

00:22:00.643 --> 00:22:02.944
We'll be sharing the details
about the Charity Pet Program

00:22:03.078 --> 00:22:05.481
on the World of Warcraft
website soon.

00:22:07.016 --> 00:22:09.785
So, we've talked quite a bit
about Shadowlands.

00:22:10.853 --> 00:22:13.222
Classic players,
now it's your turn.

00:22:13.355 --> 00:22:16.958
It's my pleasure to hand off
to my teammate Holly Longdale.

00:22:17.092 --> 00:22:18.793
She's a long-time WoW player,

00:22:18.928 --> 00:22:21.229
a veteran MMO developer,

00:22:21.363 --> 00:22:23.632
and she's going to tell us
what's in store for WoW Classic.

00:22:24.767 --> 00:22:26.902
# DRAMATIC
ORCHESTRAL MUSIC

00:22:28.037 --> 00:22:30.138
BIRDS CAWING

00:22:30.272 --> 00:22:31.073
ROARS

00:22:38.113 --> 00:22:39.214
Hi, everybody.

00:22:39.348 --> 00:22:41.716
First,
I'd like to thank all of you

00:22:41.850 --> 00:22:43.218
who have ever been part

00:22:43.352 --> 00:22:45.787
of the WoW community
over the years.

00:22:45.921 --> 00:22:47.622
You know, online worlds like WoW

00:22:47.756 --> 00:22:50.326
have been a huge part of our
lives for decades now.

00:22:51.493 --> 00:22:55.397
As a dedicated MMO fan
and a developer myself,

00:22:55.531 --> 00:22:56.899
I remember hearing

00:22:57.032 --> 00:22:59.567
that Blizzard was going to be
making their own MMO,

00:22:59.702 --> 00:23:02.370
and I thought, "Well, I guess
I'll check out that beta."

00:23:03.372 --> 00:23:04.740
And, sure,
we all call the game WoW,

00:23:04.873 --> 00:23:08.343
but really, wow!

00:23:08.477 --> 00:23:13.081
(CHUCKLES) I could not believe I
got bit by the MMO bug again.

00:23:13.215 --> 00:23:16.151
I was so excited to be able to
make a Night Elf Hunter

00:23:16.285 --> 00:23:19.254
and be like that famous
Dark Elf Ranger

00:23:19.388 --> 00:23:20.990
from the books that I loved.

00:23:21.724 --> 00:23:23.092
I have to tell you,

00:23:23.225 --> 00:23:27.763
Azeroth was, and still is,
a place I love to live.

00:23:27.896 --> 00:23:29.264
Since last year,

00:23:29.398 --> 00:23:32.501
I've had the great honor to work
alongside the WoW Classic team

00:23:32.635 --> 00:23:34.936
to bring
these nostalgic experiences

00:23:35.070 --> 00:23:38.106
back to life for long-time fans

00:23:38.240 --> 00:23:40.175
and a whole new generation
of players.

00:23:40.309 --> 00:23:43.945
As a fan myself,
I've had so much fun in WoW.

00:23:44.813 --> 00:23:47.182
From the simple things,
like drive-by buffing,

00:23:47.316 --> 00:23:49.751
or making friends
on that long haul

00:23:49.885 --> 00:23:52.287
from Teldrassil to Ironforge,

00:23:52.421 --> 00:23:55.791
all the way
to the absolutely staggering,

00:23:55.924 --> 00:23:59.128
like when I jumped blindly
through the Dark Portal

00:23:59.261 --> 00:24:01.930
and was running through
Hellfire Peninsula,

00:24:02.064 --> 00:24:04.766
heard this terrifying noise,

00:24:04.900 --> 00:24:06.968
and then saw the Fel Reaver.

00:24:07.102 --> 00:24:10.872
Biggest roamer I had ever seen,

00:24:11.006 --> 00:24:13.409
and I was very glad I had Feign
Death in that moment.

00:24:15.010 --> 00:24:16.712
And that's the thing about WoW:

00:24:16.845 --> 00:24:19.881
These stories
and experiences we all share

00:24:20.015 --> 00:24:23.118
keep us coming back
time after time.

00:24:23.719 --> 00:24:24.886
With that said,

00:24:25.020 --> 00:24:27.890
I'm super excited
to be able to share with you

00:24:28.023 --> 00:24:31.894
where our adventures
are taking us next.

00:24:33.762 --> 00:24:34.796
WIND HOWLING

00:24:34.930 --> 00:24:36.965
THUNDER RUMBLING

00:24:38.834 --> 00:24:40.903
THUNDER CRASHES

00:24:43.706 --> 00:24:45.741
THUNDER RUMBLING

00:24:46.642 --> 00:24:48.644
THUNDER CRASHES

00:24:51.180 --> 00:24:52.214
ETHEREAL HOWLING

00:24:54.783 --> 00:24:58.586
ILLIDAN STORMRAGE:
You dare enter my realm?

00:24:58.721 --> 00:24:59.688
# DRAMATIC ORCHESTRAL
MUSIC BUILDS

00:25:01.990 --> 00:25:03.258
MAGTHERIDON ROARS

00:25:10.833 --> 00:25:12.234
ORC ROARS

00:25:17.506 --> 00:25:17.806
GRUUL ROARS

00:25:24.179 --> 00:25:24.712
ELEKK BELLOWS

00:25:24.847 --> 00:25:26.515
LAUGHTER

00:25:47.169 --> 00:25:49.204
GRUUL: Gruul smash!

00:25:51.807 --> 00:25:53.175
PRINCE MALCHEZAAR:
Your foolishness

00:25:53.308 --> 00:25:55.010
has brought you to this end.

00:25:55.144 --> 00:25:58.046
MAGTHERIDON:
Take my blood and choke on it!

00:25:58.180 --> 00:25:59.348
LADY VASHJ:
Death to the outsiders!

00:26:01.683 --> 00:26:04.453
KAEL'THAS SUNSTRIDER: I'll turn
your world upside down!

00:26:09.424 --> 00:26:12.027
ILLIDAN STORMRAGE:
You are not prepared!

00:26:26.842 --> 00:26:30.312
Brings back
so many memories, right?

00:26:30.445 --> 00:26:33.148
Like exploring the fungal
forests of Zangarmarsh,

00:26:33.282 --> 00:26:35.150
or being awestruck

00:26:35.284 --> 00:26:38.187
at the chaotic magic
alive in Netherstorm.

00:26:38.954 --> 00:26:40.055
The Draenei in Exodar,

00:26:40.189 --> 00:26:42.290
the Blood Elves in Silvermoon -

00:26:42.424 --> 00:26:44.893
I loved playing them both.

00:26:45.027 --> 00:26:47.395
Do you choose to enlist
the Aldor or the Scryers

00:26:47.529 --> 00:26:49.731
in your quest
to fight the Legion?

00:26:49.865 --> 00:26:52.133
And, of course, we can't forget,

00:26:52.267 --> 00:26:54.736
gathering all your friends
to fight Illidan

00:26:54.870 --> 00:26:56.905
at the top of the Black Temple.

00:26:57.873 --> 00:26:59.508
I can't wait
to relive it all with you.

00:26:59.641 --> 00:27:03.078
Since the team first set out
on their own quest

00:27:03.212 --> 00:27:04.913
to bring the original
WoW back to life,

00:27:05.047 --> 00:27:07.182
we have learned a ton

00:27:07.316 --> 00:27:10.252
about what players are expecting
from this kind of experience.

00:27:11.220 --> 00:27:15.590
We've also learned when to keep
things just as they were,

00:27:15.724 --> 00:27:19.127
and where we all might be open
to some changes.

00:27:20.062 --> 00:27:23.498
We're bringing all these lessons
into Burning Crusade Classic,

00:27:23.632 --> 00:27:27.435
with our primary goal to bring
back the same feeling you had

00:27:27.569 --> 00:27:30.005
when you faced the Fel Reaver
for the first time,

00:27:30.138 --> 00:27:34.977
or when you were digging through
piles of Fellhound poop.

00:27:36.311 --> 00:27:37.945
Of course, we can't
get this right without you,

00:27:38.080 --> 00:27:39.748
our incredible community.

00:27:40.716 --> 00:27:43.418
Soon, you'll be able
to revisit Outland yourself

00:27:43.552 --> 00:27:44.853
when beta starts,

00:27:44.987 --> 00:27:46.788
and tell us what you think.

00:27:46.922 --> 00:27:49.624
Later, all WoW Classic players

00:27:49.758 --> 00:27:52.294
are going to be presented
with a meaningful choice

00:27:52.427 --> 00:27:55.530
for each one
of your beloved characters.

00:27:56.865 --> 00:27:59.367
Do you want to move on
into Burning Crusade Classic,

00:28:00.235 --> 00:28:04.973
or do you want to stay in the
original Classic era forever?

00:28:05.841 --> 00:28:07.209
Whatever you decide,

00:28:07.342 --> 00:28:09.977
you can do it all
with your one WoW subscription.

00:28:11.013 --> 00:28:13.448
Now, I know I've thrown
a lot at you, but don't worry.

00:28:14.249 --> 00:28:14.949
We'll be getting
into the details

00:28:15.083 --> 00:28:17.452
in our panel later today,

00:28:17.586 --> 00:28:18.887
so stick with us.

00:28:19.021 --> 00:28:21.823
We'll make sure
you are prepared.

00:28:23.292 --> 00:28:26.228
And now we're going to hear
what's coming up in Hearthstone.

00:28:27.262 --> 00:28:29.431
# FAIRGROUND MUSIC

00:28:41.510 --> 00:28:42.978
# HEARTHSTONE THEME MUSIC

00:28:43.111 --> 00:28:44.312
Greetings.

00:28:44.446 --> 00:28:47.048
We're truly excited
to share with you

00:28:47.182 --> 00:28:48.716
everything that's coming
to Hearthstone this year.

00:28:48.850 --> 00:28:51.820
But first,
let's take a quick look back

00:28:51.954 --> 00:28:52.920
at the Year of the Phoenix.

00:28:54.122 --> 00:28:58.160
We added our first new class,
the Demon Hunter,

00:28:58.293 --> 00:28:59.961
and ventured
into the ruthless Outlands.

00:29:00.862 --> 00:29:02.497
Then we went
to Scholomance Academy

00:29:02.631 --> 00:29:05.266
and got to explore
Dual-Class cards

00:29:05.400 --> 00:29:06.268
and their powerful synergies.

00:29:07.970 --> 00:29:09.671
And with our third expansion
of the year,

00:29:09.805 --> 00:29:13.174
we brought you Hearthstone's
biggest update ever,

00:29:13.308 --> 00:29:15.009
alongside the menacing Old Gods

00:29:15.143 --> 00:29:16.745
in Madness
at the Darkmoon Faire.

00:29:18.046 --> 00:29:21.449
We launched a brand-new
game mode, Duels,

00:29:21.583 --> 00:29:23.852
that saw more than ten million
matches on its first day.

00:29:25.420 --> 00:29:27.856
We also introduced our
long-awaited achievement system

00:29:27.990 --> 00:29:29.858
and made a significant overhaul

00:29:29.992 --> 00:29:32.426
to the rewards and progression
within the game.

00:29:33.562 --> 00:29:37.199
Now it's time to say farewell
to the Year of the Phoenix

00:29:37.332 --> 00:29:39.201
and see what's in store
for Hearthstone this year.

00:29:41.003 --> 00:29:43.171
Welcome
to the Year of the Griffin.

00:29:46.641 --> 00:29:47.675
Over the last couple of years

00:29:47.809 --> 00:29:50.212
we've made
big changes to Hearthstone.

00:29:50.345 --> 00:29:51.512
Throughout
the Year of the Griffin,

00:29:51.646 --> 00:29:55.384
we want to keep delivering
fun new experiences,

00:29:55.517 --> 00:29:57.952
and make sure
that the tens of millions

00:29:58.086 --> 00:29:59.620
of you playing Hearthstone

00:29:59.755 --> 00:30:01.890
are always excited to log in.

00:30:02.024 --> 00:30:03.358
First up,

00:30:03.492 --> 00:30:06.794
we'll be giving the standard
format its biggest shake-up ever

00:30:06.928 --> 00:30:10.732
with the launch of the Core Set
later this year.

00:30:10.866 --> 00:30:14.802
The Core Set replaces
the old Basic and Classic sets

00:30:14.936 --> 00:30:18.206
with a collection of 235 cards

00:30:18.340 --> 00:30:20.809
made up of some of the best
from throughout the years,

00:30:21.610 --> 00:30:25.413
as well as 29 awesome
brand-new cards.

00:30:25.547 --> 00:30:27.749
And the best thing
about the Core Set

00:30:27.883 --> 00:30:30.318
is that it's entirely free,

00:30:30.452 --> 00:30:33.654
so there's never been a better
time to get into Hearthstone.

00:30:34.556 --> 00:30:38.426
Here are three of Hearthstone's
Legendary Dragons,

00:30:38.560 --> 00:30:40.995
reimagined to feel more
up-to-date and competitive

00:30:41.129 --> 00:30:43.198
for modern-day Hearthstone.

00:30:44.399 --> 00:30:47.001
Ysera the Dreamer.

00:30:47.135 --> 00:30:49.336
You'll finally receive
her full arsenal

00:30:49.471 --> 00:30:50.838
of Dream cards right away.

00:30:51.807 --> 00:30:53.208
She's a nightmare
for your opponents.

00:30:55.977 --> 00:30:57.679
Malygos the Spellweaver.

00:30:58.580 --> 00:31:00.181
He'll fill your hand with spells

00:31:00.315 --> 00:31:01.516
and is a powerful
late-game play.

00:31:02.651 --> 00:31:06.120
Worthy of the Aspect of Magic.

00:31:06.254 --> 00:31:08.022
And finally,

00:31:08.156 --> 00:31:10.125
everyone's favorite
black dragon...

00:31:11.827 --> 00:31:12.827
Deathwing.

00:31:13.662 --> 00:31:14.862
He's still
as destructive as ever,

00:31:14.996 --> 00:31:16.531
but timed correctly,

00:31:16.665 --> 00:31:18.433
he won't leave you empty-handed.

00:31:19.568 --> 00:31:22.703
We'll also be launching
a brand-new format:

00:31:22.838 --> 00:31:24.272
Classic,

00:31:24.406 --> 00:31:25.306
where you can play Hearthstone

00:31:25.440 --> 00:31:27.875
as it was
when it first launched.

00:31:28.844 --> 00:31:31.212
The Classic format
will be fully supported,

00:31:31.346 --> 00:31:33.648
complete with ranks and rewards

00:31:33.782 --> 00:31:37.284
using Hearthstone's
original set of cards.

00:31:37.419 --> 00:31:38.620
So,

00:31:38.753 --> 00:31:41.789
if you want to relive
the old-school experience,

00:31:41.923 --> 00:31:43.791
then Classic
is the place for you.

00:31:43.925 --> 00:31:46.461
With Classic
revisiting the past,

00:31:46.595 --> 00:31:48.729
now let's take a look
to the future

00:31:48.864 --> 00:31:53.201
and explore the first expansion
of the Year of the Griffin.

00:31:54.336 --> 00:31:56.638
# OMINOUS MUSIC

00:31:56.771 --> 00:31:58.640
SAURFANG:
For a hero of the Horde...

00:32:00.609 --> 00:32:03.845
all roads lead
to the Crossroads.

00:32:05.680 --> 00:32:08.650
You have come for "adventure."

00:32:09.718 --> 00:32:13.321
But the Barrens
wants to break you.

00:32:14.890 --> 00:32:16.090
Your axe...

00:32:16.224 --> 00:32:17.158
WOLF SNARLS

00:32:17.292 --> 00:32:18.927
...must be sharp.

00:32:19.628 --> 00:32:21.229
Your wits...

00:32:22.297 --> 00:32:23.064
must be keen.

00:32:25.300 --> 00:32:25.834
And your heart...

00:32:28.236 --> 00:32:29.337
must be mighty.

00:32:35.377 --> 00:32:37.412
SNARLING

00:32:37.546 --> 00:32:39.314
SCREECHING

00:32:39.447 --> 00:32:40.482
HORN BELLOWS

00:32:43.485 --> 00:32:44.519
ORCS CHANTING

00:32:46.721 --> 00:32:48.190
SAURFANG: Strength...

00:32:49.157 --> 00:32:49.691
and honor.

00:32:51.793 --> 00:32:54.161
This is who we are.

00:32:54.296 --> 00:32:56.331
ORCS CHANTING

00:32:57.299 --> 00:32:59.367
ROKARA: For the Horde!

00:33:08.243 --> 00:33:09.410
That's right,

00:33:09.544 --> 00:33:12.180
we're headed to one of
Warcraft's most iconic locales,

00:33:12.314 --> 00:33:14.048
the Barrens,

00:33:14.182 --> 00:33:17.285
and we'll come face-to-face
with the heroes that inhabit it,

00:33:17.419 --> 00:33:20.388
starting with one of the Horde's
most iconic

00:33:20.522 --> 00:33:22.123
and well-known characters -

00:33:22.257 --> 00:33:25.360
a fierce loyalist,
one-time war chief,

00:33:25.493 --> 00:33:27.361
that embodies the honor, loyalty

00:33:27.495 --> 00:33:29.664
and spirituality of the Horde:

00:33:30.599 --> 00:33:32.901
Shadow Hunter Vol'jin.

00:33:34.169 --> 00:33:36.972
Shadow Hunter Vol'jin
is a neutral Legendary

00:33:37.105 --> 00:33:39.941
that allows you
to either bolster your own board

00:33:40.075 --> 00:33:41.910
or weaken that
of your opponent's.

00:33:42.911 --> 00:33:44.778
And to celebrate
the announcement

00:33:44.913 --> 00:33:45.647
of Forged in the Barrens,

00:33:45.780 --> 00:33:47.882
this card is available for free,

00:33:48.016 --> 00:33:50.484
for everyone, later today.

00:33:50.619 --> 00:33:52.987
So log in to Hearthstone

00:33:53.121 --> 00:33:55.223
and claim your free copy
of Shadow Hunter Vol'jin.

00:33:56.091 --> 00:33:57.993
And as a bonus...

00:33:59.361 --> 00:34:00.895
we're also giving away

00:34:01.029 --> 00:34:03.898
the brand-new
30 Years of Blizzard card back.

00:34:05.967 --> 00:34:09.137
Next, we have another hero
of the Horde,

00:34:09.271 --> 00:34:10.605
who is making his first
appearance in Hearthstone.

00:34:12.607 --> 00:34:15.477
The legendary
Blademaster Samuro,

00:34:15.610 --> 00:34:19.180
featuring
the new keyword Frenzy.

00:34:20.048 --> 00:34:21.516
Frenzy activates the first time

00:34:21.650 --> 00:34:24.585
a minion takes damage
and survives.

00:34:24.719 --> 00:34:26.087
In Samuro's case,

00:34:26.221 --> 00:34:29.090
this can be used
to clear your opponent's board.

00:34:29.224 --> 00:34:31.159
Heroes of the Horde,
like Samuro,

00:34:31.293 --> 00:34:33.527
are famous
for their combat prowess,

00:34:33.662 --> 00:34:34.729
but others, like Thrall,

00:34:34.863 --> 00:34:37.365
are known for their powerful
elemental magic.

00:34:40.135 --> 00:34:43.071
Take a look at this new Shaman
spell, Chain Lightning.

00:34:43.905 --> 00:34:45.573
Chain Lightning is a spell

00:34:45.707 --> 00:34:47.508
in a new cycle of cards
that rank up

00:34:47.642 --> 00:34:50.211
and become more powerful
when you have 5 and 10 mana,

00:34:52.247 --> 00:34:54.615
ensuring
that they're always useful

00:34:54.749 --> 00:34:56.251
at every stage in the game.

00:34:59.154 --> 00:35:02.857
You'll also notice that they're
categorized as Nature spells.

00:35:02.991 --> 00:35:04.092
With Forged in the Barrens,

00:35:04.225 --> 00:35:06.360
we'll be permanently introducing
spell schools

00:35:06.494 --> 00:35:08.529
across the entire game,

00:35:08.663 --> 00:35:13.201
which enables a whole host
of exciting new strategies.

00:35:13.335 --> 00:35:15.537
And don't worry,
members of the Alliance.

00:35:15.670 --> 00:35:19.140
We'll be featuring
some of your most beloved heroes

00:35:19.274 --> 00:35:21.710
and locales later this year.

00:35:23.178 --> 00:35:26.313
But what I love most
about the Warcraft universe

00:35:26.448 --> 00:35:28.615
is its amazing characters,

00:35:28.750 --> 00:35:30.050
and our final announcement

00:35:30.185 --> 00:35:32.653
is our most ambitious addition
to Hearthstone yet.

00:35:32.787 --> 00:35:35.556
It introduces a brand-new way
to play

00:35:35.690 --> 00:35:36.391
with your favorite heroes.

00:35:37.425 --> 00:35:39.627
Hearthstone Mercenaries.

00:35:41.930 --> 00:35:44.632
Mercenaries features
strategic RPG gameplay,

00:35:44.766 --> 00:35:46.467
where you build teams

00:35:46.601 --> 00:35:49.404
consisting of some of the most
iconic heroes and villains

00:35:49.537 --> 00:35:51.639
from the Warcraft universe.

00:35:51.773 --> 00:35:54.409
Including timeless characters

00:35:54.542 --> 00:35:56.911
like the infamous
Sylvanas Windrunner...

00:35:58.179 --> 00:36:01.883
and Ragnaros,
the Elemental Lord of Fire.

00:36:02.784 --> 00:36:05.987
You can also expect to see some
of Hearthstone's fan favorites,

00:36:06.121 --> 00:36:09.491
like the unstoppable Devilsaur,
King Krush,

00:36:10.692 --> 00:36:13.661
and the ever-growing
Gruul the Dragonslayer.

00:36:14.963 --> 00:36:16.264
You'll lead them in battle

00:36:16.398 --> 00:36:18.599
through highly replayable
roguelike missions,

00:36:18.733 --> 00:36:23.104
where the map is randomly
generated every time you play,

00:36:23.238 --> 00:36:25.506
and each node represents
a unique challenge

00:36:25.640 --> 00:36:27.508
for your team to take on.

00:36:27.642 --> 00:36:31.345
Your heroes gain levels,
new abilities, equipment,

00:36:31.479 --> 00:36:35.282
and can even evolve into more
powerful versions of themselves.

00:36:36.484 --> 00:36:38.586
We're thrilled to finally show
you Hearthstone Mercenaries.

00:36:38.720 --> 00:36:41.656
It is scheduled to launch
later this year,

00:36:41.790 --> 00:36:45.025
and we'll have more to share
with you down the road.

00:36:45.160 --> 00:36:48.529
Everything you've seen today
is just a taste of what's coming

00:36:48.663 --> 00:36:49.530
in the Year of the Griffin,

00:36:50.498 --> 00:36:53.101
so don't forget to tune in
to our deep-dive panel

00:36:53.234 --> 00:36:55.102
after the Opening Ceremony,

00:36:55.236 --> 00:36:58.205
where we'll share more details
on the Core Set,

00:36:58.339 --> 00:36:59.207
the new Classic format,

00:36:59.340 --> 00:37:00.775
Forged in the Barrens,

00:37:00.909 --> 00:37:04.011
and our plans
for Battlegrounds and Duels,

00:37:04.145 --> 00:37:05.647
as well as our upcoming
single-player content.

00:37:06.581 --> 00:37:09.517
I want to thank the team
for their amazing work.

00:37:09.651 --> 00:37:12.286
And on behalf of all of us
at Hearthstone,

00:37:12.420 --> 00:37:14.355
we want to thank
the many millions of you

00:37:14.489 --> 00:37:15.790
who play our game.

00:37:16.758 --> 00:37:18.225
Your dedication and support

00:37:18.359 --> 00:37:20.728
is what drives us
to make awesome updates

00:37:20.862 --> 00:37:23.798
and pursue ambitious
and fun ideas.

00:37:23.932 --> 00:37:25.633
We can't wait to kick off
the Year of the Griffin

00:37:25.767 --> 00:37:28.136
with all of you,

00:37:28.269 --> 00:37:30.071
and we hope to see you
in the game soon.

00:37:31.473 --> 00:37:34.642
Next up, you'll get an update
on all things Diablo.

00:37:35.844 --> 00:37:37.979
ROARS

00:37:38.112 --> 00:37:39.581
# DRAMATIC ORCHESTRAL MUSIC

00:37:49.357 --> 00:37:50.391
Hey, everyone.

00:37:50.525 --> 00:37:53.160
Thank you very much
for joining us.

00:37:53.294 --> 00:37:57.732
I am so excited to kick off
the Diablo segment of our show,

00:37:57.866 --> 00:37:59.400
and I am honored to be here

00:37:59.534 --> 00:38:01.669
on behalf of all
of our Diablo teams

00:38:01.803 --> 00:38:04.838
to share the news and updates
we have in store for you today.

00:38:05.773 --> 00:38:07.742
We've got a lot
of Diablo to cover,

00:38:07.876 --> 00:38:09.810
and I hope you'll agree with me

00:38:09.944 --> 00:38:11.646
that it's a great time to be a
member of this community.

00:38:12.947 --> 00:38:15.349
Alright, let's kick things off
with Diablo IV.

00:38:16.384 --> 00:38:20.922
We first shared our game with
you during BlizzCon of 2019,

00:38:21.055 --> 00:38:22.757
and we've been truly humbled
by your response.

00:38:23.992 --> 00:38:26.260
We've kept in touch
through quarterly updates,

00:38:26.394 --> 00:38:28.595
and sincerely appreciate
the thoughts

00:38:28.730 --> 00:38:30.531
and valuable feedback
you've provided

00:38:30.665 --> 00:38:33.267
as we unveil more
and more of the game

00:38:33.401 --> 00:38:35.136
and share in its development.

00:38:36.304 --> 00:38:39.340
After all, Diablo belongs to you
as much as it belongs to us.

00:38:41.309 --> 00:38:46.013
Most recently, we teased an
update to our campfire screen,

00:38:46.147 --> 00:38:47.581
and savvy fans,
of course, understood

00:38:47.715 --> 00:38:49.850
that we meant more than just
the character lighting

00:38:49.984 --> 00:38:52.119
and fire visual effects.

00:38:53.087 --> 00:38:55.856
That's right,
today we're happy to announce

00:38:55.990 --> 00:38:57.858
a brave new soul
joining the Barbarian,

00:38:57.992 --> 00:39:00.628
the Sorcerer and the Druid

00:39:00.762 --> 00:39:02.797
on this dangerous journey
back to Sanctuary.

00:39:03.765 --> 00:39:06.768
A class is one
of the most exciting things

00:39:06.901 --> 00:39:07.869
that you can announce
in a Diablo game.

00:39:09.671 --> 00:39:12.373
This one is especially
exciting to me,

00:39:12.507 --> 00:39:15.709
as it's a re-envisioning
of one of the first classes

00:39:15.843 --> 00:39:17.044
to ever appear in the series.

00:39:17.178 --> 00:39:18.279
Let's have a look.

00:39:22.951 --> 00:39:25.152
# SOMBER ORCHESTRAL MUSIC

00:39:25.286 --> 00:39:27.989
PRIEST: Your prayers do not fall
on deaf ears.

00:39:30.959 --> 00:39:33.728
Just know they are being heard.

00:39:36.764 --> 00:39:39.033
There is justice
within the Light...

00:39:40.435 --> 00:39:41.869
but you have to be patient.

00:39:44.772 --> 00:39:47.875
Now, pray with me.

00:39:49.510 --> 00:39:52.580
May Akarat guide and protect me.

00:39:53.715 --> 00:39:57.484
PARISHIONER:
May Akarat guide and protect me.

00:39:57.619 --> 00:40:00.654
May he shepherd my soul...

00:40:00.788 --> 00:40:02.390
May he shepherd my soul...

00:40:03.157 --> 00:40:06.661
...and grant it mercy.

00:40:06.794 --> 00:40:07.828
APPROACHING FOOTSTEPS

00:40:07.962 --> 00:40:09.831
...and grant it mercy.

00:40:10.798 --> 00:40:13.067
What are you doing here?

00:40:13.201 --> 00:40:14.902
This is not the time.

00:40:15.970 --> 00:40:17.405
But this is confession.

00:40:20.408 --> 00:40:22.677
And I have sinned.

00:40:25.246 --> 00:40:26.948
I was a thief...

00:40:28.182 --> 00:40:30.351
who stole
from those more fortunate.

00:40:32.120 --> 00:40:32.286
COINS JINGLE

00:40:34.822 --> 00:40:36.624
I strayed from your Light...

00:40:37.725 --> 00:40:40.828
and found my trade
in the Shadows.

00:40:44.666 --> 00:40:46.934
They call it murder.

00:40:48.069 --> 00:40:51.906
I say job well done.

00:40:52.040 --> 00:40:52.707
GRUNTS

00:40:54.242 --> 00:40:55.743
GROANS

00:40:58.646 --> 00:40:58.980
PRIEST: Stop.

00:40:59.781 --> 00:41:00.815
Stop!

00:41:01.616 --> 00:41:01.716
Enough!

00:41:05.520 --> 00:41:06.554
ROGUE: I am a thief...

00:41:08.122 --> 00:41:08.723
a heretic...

00:41:10.358 --> 00:41:12.226
a murderer, Father.

00:41:14.028 --> 00:41:16.230
Will Akarat save me?

00:41:19.033 --> 00:41:20.068
PRIEST GRUNTS

00:41:21.035 --> 00:41:22.570
You mock our Light...

00:41:24.706 --> 00:41:27.842
but those monsters
were a scourge upon my flock.

00:41:29.043 --> 00:41:31.245
And you... (SCOFFS)

00:41:33.548 --> 00:41:35.750
...you were the answer
to their prayers.

00:41:38.219 --> 00:41:39.087
ROGUE: Then we are settled.

00:41:40.221 --> 00:41:41.556
And you owe me.

00:41:43.858 --> 00:41:46.728
The name you seek is...
(INDISTINCT WHISPERING)

00:41:50.865 --> 00:41:52.233
Thank the Heavens for you.

00:41:54.469 --> 00:41:54.535
Heavens?

00:41:56.137 --> 00:41:57.438
I assure you, Father...

00:41:59.140 --> 00:42:01.041
the Heavens didn't send me.

00:42:01.175 --> 00:42:03.177
# DRAMATIC ORCHESTRAL MUSIC

00:42:08.816 --> 00:42:10.852
FIGHTING GRUNTS

00:42:55.329 --> 00:42:56.364
# SOMBER ORCHESTRAL MUSIC

00:43:16.284 --> 00:43:17.385
DOORS SLAM

00:43:21.856 --> 00:43:24.825
Just the sound of that ear
getting pierced

00:43:24.959 --> 00:43:26.226
by the hook is so brutal.

00:43:26.360 --> 00:43:28.829
I feel like it's going to
haunt me for a long time.

00:43:28.963 --> 00:43:30.831
I've been a huge fan
of the Rogue

00:43:30.965 --> 00:43:32.099
ever since the original Diablo.

00:43:32.900 --> 00:43:36.337
Even seeing them come back
as NPCs and Mercenaries

00:43:36.470 --> 00:43:38.772
in Diablo II's Rogue Encampment

00:43:38.906 --> 00:43:41.175
served as a great bridge
between the games.

00:43:42.476 --> 00:43:44.512
With the setting of Diablo IV
being a larger world

00:43:44.645 --> 00:43:46.646
than we've ever
played in before,

00:43:46.781 --> 00:43:48.249
we're excited to show you

00:43:48.382 --> 00:43:50.317
not just what the successors

00:43:50.451 --> 00:43:52.753
to the original Rogues
in the series

00:43:52.887 --> 00:43:54.755
have been up to
since the fall of their order,

00:43:54.889 --> 00:43:56.824
but also what some
of the other Rogues

00:43:56.958 --> 00:43:58.693
in the world of Sanctuary
might look like.

00:43:59.627 --> 00:44:04.932
The mantra for Diablo IV has
been "customization first,"

00:44:05.066 --> 00:44:07.034
and the Rogue takes this
to a whole new level.

00:44:07.835 --> 00:44:09.103
From the beginning,

00:44:09.237 --> 00:44:12.706
the Rogue has been
an incredibly flexible class,

00:44:12.840 --> 00:44:14.875
able to adapt to any situation.

00:44:15.009 --> 00:44:17.445
Our goal is to let you create

00:44:17.578 --> 00:44:19.247
the kind of Rogue
that you want to play,

00:44:20.248 --> 00:44:22.282
whether it's
an unrivalled archer

00:44:22.416 --> 00:44:24.852
modelled after
the original Sisterhood,

00:44:24.986 --> 00:44:27.021
or a cloak-and-dagger Rogue

00:44:27.154 --> 00:44:29.957
from the darkest
alleys of Caldeum.

00:44:30.091 --> 00:44:32.793
In Diablo IV,
you will have the freedom

00:44:32.927 --> 00:44:34.628
to create
the Rogue that you imagine,

00:44:34.762 --> 00:44:38.132
by customizing the looks,
the background

00:44:38.266 --> 00:44:39.967
and the playstyle
of your character.

00:44:41.002 --> 00:44:44.371
Please stick around
for our segment later today,

00:44:44.505 --> 00:44:46.974
where I'll be joined by other
members of the Diablo IV team

00:44:47.108 --> 00:44:49.376
to share a closer look
at the Rogue class,

00:44:49.510 --> 00:44:52.780
as well as some
of the open-world gameplay

00:44:52.914 --> 00:44:53.981
that we're bringing to the game.

00:44:54.115 --> 00:44:55.283
Spoilers:

00:44:55.416 --> 00:44:57.285
those severed ears
are not just for show.

00:44:59.420 --> 00:45:01.221
But Diablo IV

00:45:01.355 --> 00:45:04.224
is not the only Diablo game
we're talking about today.

00:45:04.358 --> 00:45:06.827
If you're looking
for an authentic

00:45:06.961 --> 00:45:08.496
Diablo experience on mobile,

00:45:08.629 --> 00:45:09.664
we've got you covered.

00:45:11.032 --> 00:45:12.899
Diablo Immortal has everything
you'd expect

00:45:13.034 --> 00:45:15.402
from an AAA action-RPG,

00:45:15.536 --> 00:45:18.405
from the visceral combat
and epic loot,

00:45:18.539 --> 00:45:20.908
to an all-new story

00:45:21.042 --> 00:45:22.643
bridging the gap
between the events

00:45:22.777 --> 00:45:24.145
of Diablo II and Diablo III.

00:45:25.780 --> 00:45:27.915
Later today
you can join the Immortal team,

00:45:28.049 --> 00:45:31.252
where they'll talk about some of
the things they've learned

00:45:31.385 --> 00:45:33.520
from the recent alpha test,
and what's next for the game.

00:45:33.654 --> 00:45:35.756
But that's still not all.

00:45:35.890 --> 00:45:39.427
We have one last bit of very
exciting Diablo news to cover.

00:45:40.795 --> 00:45:43.931
When you hear us talk
about the classes,

00:45:44.065 --> 00:45:47.334
the items or the stories
of the early Diablo games,

00:45:47.468 --> 00:45:48.669
you may have picked up

00:45:48.803 --> 00:45:52.005
on the absolute reverent
tone we reserve

00:45:52.139 --> 00:45:53.708
for that golden era of Diablo.

00:45:55.042 --> 00:45:57.744
Maybe you share
that love of the classics,

00:45:57.878 --> 00:45:59.346
and just hearing us
talk about them

00:45:59.480 --> 00:46:01.515
makes you want
to take on Mephisto

00:46:01.649 --> 00:46:04.685
or Baal one more time, or maybe
even for the first time.

00:46:04.819 --> 00:46:07.120
After all,

00:46:07.254 --> 00:46:09.690
some of our favorite moments
happened a long time ago,

00:46:09.824 --> 00:46:11.292
and not just in Sanctuary years.

00:46:13.094 --> 00:46:16.630
If so, we have a special
surprise for you today.

00:46:16.764 --> 00:46:17.631
Let's check it out.

00:46:22.503 --> 00:46:24.538
ETHEREAL WHISPERING

00:46:24.672 --> 00:46:27.107
BAAL: How was it not your fault?

00:46:27.241 --> 00:46:29.610
MARIUS: The Wanderer...

00:46:29.744 --> 00:46:31.611
THE WANDERER: Now you know
what I seek, Marius.

00:46:31.746 --> 00:46:32.813
BAAL: Enough!

00:46:32.947 --> 00:46:35.115
MARIUS: Were these the demons
from my dream?

00:46:35.249 --> 00:46:36.283
TYRAEL: Don't do it!

00:46:36.417 --> 00:46:37.150
BAAL: It seems your terms...

00:46:37.284 --> 00:46:38.385
TYRAEL: Fool!

00:46:38.519 --> 00:46:40.721
BAAL: ...are not acceptable.

00:46:40.855 --> 00:46:41.888
TAL RASHA:
Look what they've done to me.

00:46:42.023 --> 00:46:44.325
MEPHISTO: Arise, Diablo,

00:46:45.593 --> 00:46:47.294
Lord of Terror!

00:46:47.428 --> 00:46:49.463
# SOMBER MUSIC

00:46:55.002 --> 00:46:56.203
TYRAEL: Though this be
our darkest hour...

00:46:57.938 --> 00:47:00.174
it may yet
be your greatest moment.

00:47:14.221 --> 00:47:15.423
BARBARIAN ROARS

00:47:34.775 --> 00:47:36.844
# OMINOUS ORCHESTRAL MUSIC

00:47:47.888 --> 00:47:49.423
WEREWOLF SNARLS

00:47:59.133 --> 00:48:02.403
DIABLO: Not even death
can save you from me.

00:48:10.678 --> 00:48:13.213
After more than 20 years,

00:48:13.347 --> 00:48:15.216
the Dark Wanderer has returned.

00:48:16.350 --> 00:48:18.719
And once again,
he travels east -

00:48:18.853 --> 00:48:21.388
always east.

00:48:22.256 --> 00:48:24.792
Diablo II is a landmark game
for Blizzard.

00:48:25.993 --> 00:48:30.296
Diablo II: Resurrected
is a full-HD remaster

00:48:30.431 --> 00:48:32.799
of both the original game

00:48:32.933 --> 00:48:36.003
and the expansion,
Lord of Destruction.

00:48:36.937 --> 00:48:40.441
It takes the 2D, sprite-based
classic that we love

00:48:40.574 --> 00:48:43.711
and brings it into
the present in 3D,

00:48:43.844 --> 00:48:46.146
utilizing up-to-date
graphical rendering

00:48:46.280 --> 00:48:48.382
and lighting technologies.

00:48:48.516 --> 00:48:54.654
It also includes modernizing
all 27 minutes of cinematics,

00:48:54.788 --> 00:48:57.056
recreated shot for shot,

00:48:57.191 --> 00:49:00.794
with the explicit intention
of preserving both the look

00:49:00.928 --> 00:49:03.831
and the pacing
of the original movies.

00:49:03.964 --> 00:49:08.735
Blizzard has a long history
of games that we're proud of,

00:49:08.869 --> 00:49:10.804
and when we think
about Diablo II,

00:49:10.938 --> 00:49:13.240
we think about it
as a definitive pillar

00:49:13.374 --> 00:49:14.675
in our foundation.

00:49:16.377 --> 00:49:18.679
Now, it's funny to think

00:49:18.812 --> 00:49:21.682
that some of you weren't even
born when DII was released,

00:49:21.815 --> 00:49:24.184
which makes it
all the more important

00:49:24.318 --> 00:49:26.586
that we deliver
an authentic experience,

00:49:26.720 --> 00:49:28.855
wherever you play.

00:49:28.989 --> 00:49:32.426
We want everyone
to relive their memories,

00:49:32.560 --> 00:49:35.095
or experience the game
for the very first time,

00:49:35.229 --> 00:49:36.596
on their platform of choice.

00:49:37.731 --> 00:49:40.834
And so we're excited
to bring Diablo II: Resurrected

00:49:40.968 --> 00:49:44.337
to PC and console,

00:49:44.471 --> 00:49:45.673
along with cross-progression.

00:49:47.908 --> 00:49:50.443
And for those of you who are in
love with the original

00:49:50.578 --> 00:49:53.513
and you just wish
it worked more seamlessly

00:49:53.647 --> 00:49:56.116
on modern computers,

00:49:56.250 --> 00:49:58.518
you can bring back all
of that nostalgia

00:49:58.652 --> 00:50:00.187
exactly as you remember,

00:50:00.321 --> 00:50:01.622
and enjoy the game
in its original 2D form,

00:50:03.324 --> 00:50:08.295
Later today, Diablo speedrunner
MrLlama will host a roundtable

00:50:08.429 --> 00:50:09.463
with members
of the development team

00:50:09.597 --> 00:50:12.399
on the dedicated Diablo channel.

00:50:13.434 --> 00:50:16.170
If you are a Diablo II fan,
I encourage you to take a look.

00:50:18.872 --> 00:50:22.309
So, from Diablo II: Resurrected

00:50:22.443 --> 00:50:24.711
to Burning Crusade Classic,

00:50:24.845 --> 00:50:27.313
to the Blizzard
Arcade Collection,

00:50:27.448 --> 00:50:28.549
that's a whole
lot of looking back.

00:50:30.184 --> 00:50:32.485
And while we have teams
dedicated

00:50:32.620 --> 00:50:34.821
to bringing
these timeless experiences

00:50:34.955 --> 00:50:36.389
into your hands,

00:50:36.523 --> 00:50:39.592
it's actually a very small
percentage of our developers

00:50:39.727 --> 00:50:41.495
working on these projects.

00:50:42.563 --> 00:50:46.934
Far more people are working
on the future of Blizzard.

00:50:47.067 --> 00:50:50.437
And in addition to what we'll be
talking about during the show,

00:50:50.571 --> 00:50:54.441
we can't wait to tell you even
more about our plans

00:50:54.575 --> 00:50:56.744
over the course
of this year and beyond.

00:50:58.045 --> 00:51:00.413
If you had asked us 30 years ago

00:51:00.547 --> 00:51:01.848
what gaming
would look like today,

00:51:01.982 --> 00:51:04.017
none of us could have predicted

00:51:04.151 --> 00:51:05.953
the current
Blizzard lineup of games.

00:51:06.086 --> 00:51:08.789
The advances in technology
are one thing,

00:51:08.922 --> 00:51:11.625
but it's really
what those advances have enabled

00:51:11.759 --> 00:51:14.027
that's even more incredible.

00:51:14.161 --> 00:51:15.462
If you think about
the people who play games

00:51:15.596 --> 00:51:18.465
and the communities
that have grown up around them,

00:51:18.599 --> 00:51:20.700
the way people
can connect instantly,

00:51:20.834 --> 00:51:23.370
no matter where they are
in the world,

00:51:23.504 --> 00:51:27.874
the way people are increasingly
able to express their identity

00:51:28.008 --> 00:51:31.645
and celebrate who they are

00:51:31.779 --> 00:51:34.380
through their favorite games,
communities

00:51:34.515 --> 00:51:35.449
and platforms,

00:51:35.582 --> 00:51:39.052
the explosion of things
like streaming,

00:51:39.186 --> 00:51:41.555
cosplay and esports,

00:51:41.689 --> 00:51:42.889
it would have been hard
to imagine

00:51:43.023 --> 00:51:45.292
any of that 30 years ago.

00:51:46.360 --> 00:51:47.795
And at Blizzard,

00:51:47.928 --> 00:51:50.463
that is what excites us
about the next 30 years.

00:51:51.432 --> 00:51:55.068
There is so much
that we're working on,

00:51:55.202 --> 00:51:57.805
and some of it
you already know about.

00:51:58.372 --> 00:51:59.473
The rest?

00:51:59.606 --> 00:52:01.041
We look forward
to talking to you

00:52:01.175 --> 00:52:03.143
about it when the time is right.

00:52:04.945 --> 00:52:06.313
Just like the real world,

00:52:06.447 --> 00:52:09.549
the worlds of Warcraft, Diablo,

00:52:09.683 --> 00:52:11.885
StarCraft, Heroes of the Storm,

00:52:12.019 --> 00:52:15.255
Overwatch and Hearthstone
are diverse,

00:52:15.389 --> 00:52:18.925
expansive and full of potential.

00:52:19.059 --> 00:52:21.594
We are not only iterating

00:52:21.729 --> 00:52:23.831
on the experiences that you've
come to expect from us.

00:52:24.898 --> 00:52:29.403
We're also exploring different
ways to express our worlds,

00:52:29.536 --> 00:52:33.673
and welcome more players
from more places into them.

00:52:33.807 --> 00:52:36.309
And we aspire
to continue to lead

00:52:36.443 --> 00:52:40.747
on priorities like accessibility
and toxicity control,

00:52:40.881 --> 00:52:43.150
and to continue
supporting causes

00:52:43.283 --> 00:52:45.785
that have a positive impact
on the real world.

00:52:46.820 --> 00:52:49.589
We want to continue to bring
those same feelings

00:52:49.723 --> 00:52:51.858
of joy and achievement

00:52:51.992 --> 00:52:54.194
that we all felt when we first
defeated the Lich King,

00:52:55.496 --> 00:52:57.431
or beat Diablo on Hardcore mode,

00:52:58.932 --> 00:53:03.503
because when we geek-out on
those experiences with others,

00:53:03.637 --> 00:53:06.440
we can't help but see
the similarities between us

00:53:06.573 --> 00:53:09.943
and feel what's possible
when we play together.

00:53:10.077 --> 00:53:13.013
Of course,
there are new Blizzard worlds

00:53:13.147 --> 00:53:15.382
that we haven't visited
quite yet.

00:53:17.684 --> 00:53:21.788
And when we do finally unveil
those games and experiences,

00:53:21.922 --> 00:53:25.125
our hope is that you will see in
them what we do -

00:53:25.259 --> 00:53:28.628
that no matter who you are
or where you're from,

00:53:28.762 --> 00:53:32.366
they are spaces where you can
create new stories,

00:53:32.499 --> 00:53:34.367
forge new friendships,

00:53:34.501 --> 00:53:37.371
and make memories
worthy of lasting a lifetime.

00:53:39.339 --> 00:53:42.709
And through it all,
our mission statement

00:53:42.843 --> 00:53:45.278
of being "dedicated to creating

00:53:45.412 --> 00:53:48.649
the most epic entertainment
experiences... ever,"

00:53:48.782 --> 00:53:52.152
along with our core values,
led by "gameplay first,"

00:53:52.286 --> 00:53:53.720
will continue to guide our way.

00:53:54.888 --> 00:53:57.391
So, on behalf of everyone
at Blizzard,

00:53:57.524 --> 00:53:59.660
thank you for being
on this journey.

00:54:01.361 --> 00:54:01.861
For me, personally,

00:54:03.030 --> 00:54:07.066
it is the honor of my
professional life to serve you,

00:54:07.201 --> 00:54:09.803
and the honor of all
of us at Blizzard

00:54:09.937 --> 00:54:13.073
to be the caretakers
of the worlds that you play in.

00:54:14.208 --> 00:54:16.910
We are so excited
for what's to come this year,

00:54:18.045 --> 00:54:22.015
next year,
and the next 30 years.

00:54:22.149 --> 00:54:24.251
Now,
what's coming next for the show?

00:54:25.486 --> 00:54:29.356
Well,
it depends on where you watch.

00:54:30.324 --> 00:54:33.660
For those of you looking
for an update on Overwatch,

00:54:33.794 --> 00:54:35.995
check out the
behind-the-scenes look

00:54:36.129 --> 00:54:38.565
into the development
of Overwatch 2

00:54:38.699 --> 00:54:41.067
over on their dedicated channel,

00:54:41.201 --> 00:54:43.170
right after the conclusion
of opening ceremonies.

00:54:43.303 --> 00:54:46.405
There,
you'll hear about Overwatch 2,

00:54:46.540 --> 00:54:49.509
new content, new features,

00:54:49.643 --> 00:54:53.780
including new maps,
Hero Missions, Talent trees,

00:54:53.914 --> 00:54:55.848
and more of what we think will
make Overwatch II

00:54:55.983 --> 00:54:57.684
a unique gameplay experience.

00:54:57.818 --> 00:55:01.621
For World of Warcraft,
Diablo and Hearthstone,

00:55:01.755 --> 00:55:05.125
you'll get a closer look
on their respective channels.

00:55:06.293 --> 00:55:09.029
And on the dedicated
strategy channel,

00:55:09.162 --> 00:55:12.031
some StarCraft legends
will be going head-to-head

00:55:12.165 --> 00:55:13.633
in epic competition.

00:55:14.568 --> 00:55:16.937
Once again,
welcome to BlizzConline.

00:55:18.505 --> 00:55:19.139
Be good to one another.

00:55:20.107 --> 00:55:20.307
Welcome home.

00:55:22.342 --> 00:55:24.544
Before we kick things off,

00:55:24.678 --> 00:55:27.147
here's a little something from a
previous BlizzCon headliner.

